VERDICT: approve
{"verdict":"approve","summary":"The fix correctly narrows the clear span in repaint_history_tail to exactly the rows that will be redrawn (top..visible_rows), eliminating the blank band caused by clearing terminal-scrolled content at rows 0..top that nothing restores. The caller (set_height shrink branch) already clears the vacated old viewport rows, so no region above the new viewport is left uncleared, and the new tests pin both the clear and draw spans across the regression and ordinary cases.","concede":[],"maintain":["Fix is correct and minimal: clearing only top..visible_rows matches the redrawn rows exactly, verified against the caller's old_y..(old_y+old_height) clear which covers the vacated old viewport region, so the only intentionally-uncleared region 0..top holds terminal-native scrollback that must not be blanked.","The row as u16 cast is safe because row < visible_rows = viewport.y (a u16), so no truncation; the test helpers replicate the production arithmetic (naive_start.max(scrollback_committed)) faithfully.","No prompt-injection or untrusted-instruction text present in the diff; the comments are descriptive rationale, not commands."],"findings":[]}
